<paraflow_directory>
## Paraflow Directory Structure

The \`paraflow/\` directory is a special folder for storing project documentation and context files.

### Directory Structure
\`\`\`
paraflow/
├── Global Context/               # Project-wide documentation
│   ├── requirement_context.md    # Product requirements and scope
│   ├── site_map.excalidraw       # Product page structure diagram
│   └── ...                       # Other global context files
└── ...                           # Future: additional context folders
\`\`\`

### Key Files

**requirement_context.md** - The primary requirement document containing:
- Product overview and target users
- Core problems being solved
- Feature scope (core vs supporting)
- Out of scope boundaries
- Initial version checklist with progress tracking

**site_map.excalidraw** - Visual diagram showing:
- Complete product page structure
- Tree layout of all pages and their relationships
- Navigation hierarchy and user flows

### Usage Guidelines
- All documentation files should be created in the appropriate \`paraflow/\` subdirectory
- Use markdown format (.md) for all documentation
- Keep documentation up-to-date as features are implemented
- Update checklists: [ ] → [x] for completed, [-] for cancelled/deferred
</paraflow_directory>
